  "outstanding_review": "Per-batch maceration and distillation dates for VAT28+ are 'derived' (inherited from the recorded VAT-fill/bottling date) except where a specific step date was recoverable from context (see notes on individual records). The Production!! tab's date column mixes literal dd/mm/yyyy strings with spreadsheet date serials that are sometimes day/month-swapped -- each serial in this manifest was resolved by chronological fit against its neighbours and, where available, an already founder-confirmed date (e.g. WB-022's VAT47 bottling), not by a single global format assumption. 2026-09-18: VAT56 imported (see its own notes for the bottling-date resolution) -- its earlier unlabelled '26 bottles' line is superseded, not a separate batch. VAT57/58/59 remain genuinely IN-PROGRESS batches (VAT55 completed 2026-09-18, founder-confirmed bottling 2026-08-27, 78.5 bottles) (distilled and filled, not yet bottled) using the new pending-step mechanism (ProductionBatch.pending_steps, a manifest step spec of {'pending': true}) -- the API-replay path completes only the steps that have really happened and leaves bottling/labelling PENDING in the target, same as a real user mid-process; re-edit each record's bottling step once a real bottling row appears in the sheet, then re-run replay to complete it. Only the API-replay path (scripts/whistlebird_replay.py) supports this -- the ORM-direct --rebuild-whistlebird-test path skips a pending batch entirely rather than falsely complete it (see apply_production_batches). VAT52 remains excluded: two distinct sub-issues conflated under one number (see excluded[] entry), a genuine labelling ambiguity, not simple in-progress status -- needs founder disambiguation, not a pending marker. Green Gold (gg01) is a separately recorded final-product diversion from aged Wildflower VAT53: row 2035 (2026-07-31) records 41L becoming 144 x 500ml bottles, but the founder confirmed 126 bottles were made (2026-09-20), so the modelled draw is 35.875L; the remaining 19.825L becomes 28.3214 700ml Wildflower bottles (21 original + 7.3214 additional) so VAT53 drains to zero at storage precision. Rosella VAT26 (prior database, pre-Solstice) still needs founder confirmation that treating its RS01/RS02 flavour rows as the maceration step (no Solstice base to draw from that early) is the right call. 2026-09-23: VAT37's Wildflower bottling was missing entirely (empty bottlings, unlike its neighbours VAT36 and VAT38) and wasn't flagged in excluded[] or noted above as a known gap -- it was simply missed during curation, spotted via a '-' in the sourcemap's bottled/final-product columns for an otherwise-complete batch. Founder-confirmed directly (not from a located sheet row): bottled 2025-10-23, 78 bottles -- sits between VAT36 (2025-10-16, 78 bottles) and VAT38 (2025-11-25, 78.5 bottles), which is why label-batch numbering for every later Wildflower bottling needed recomputing (see scripts/whistlebird_replay_timeline.py's _assign_label_batches) once this was added, not just VAT37's own row. 2026-09-23: VAT35's Solstice bottling was the same kind of unflagged gap (empty bottlings, no excluded[]/notes entry, aged 2025-09-02 same as VAT34 but never bottled) -- founder-confirmed directly: bottled 2025-10-09, 61 bottles, between VAT34/VAT32 (2025-09-18/2025-09-02) and VAT39 (2025-11-25).",
